/* quire_matmul_perf_golden_cases.h — baked golden (SAMPLED) for the exact
 * 256-bit b-posit16 quire MULTI-CORE-PERF MATMUL  C[N,N] = A[N,K] . B[K,N]
 * (N=128, K=64): 16384 output elements, each an EXACT-quire dot of length K,
 * distributed across the full ~140-core Blackhole baby-core grid (1048576
 * exact bp16 products total). The device computes the FULL matmul and the host
 * TIMES it; correctness is gated on a SAMPLE of S outputs spread across the
 * grid (the Fraction oracle is too slow to gate all N*N*K products).
 *
 * DO NOT hand-edit the numbers — GENERATED from the canonical oracle and
 * re-verified by the host program at startup against the reused
 * bp16_quire.h / bp16_encode.h headers (belt-and-suspenders, on the sample).
 *
 * SOURCE OF TRUTH (regenerate, never by hand):
 *   oracle: mosyne-bposit/kernels/bposit16_reference.py
 *   generator: gen_matmul_perf_golden.py (kept with this commit)
 *   cross-checked vs golden/bp16_mul.json (operand pairs that overlap)
 *
 * Layout: A is N*K row-major, B is K*N row-major, C is N*N row-major.
 * C[i,j] = Sum_k A[i*K+k] * B[k*N+j], each product EXACT (no per-product
 * rounding) into one quire; q256_add is exact => K-accumulation order-
 * independent (forward == reverse, verified on the sample). Only the per-output
 * quire->bp16 readout rounds (truncation).
 */
